<h1>Terms<br />of use.</h1>
<p>Last updated August 28, 2026. These terms cover the Infinite Pixelboard website and the iOS app.</p>

<h2>The service</h2>
<p>Infinite Pixelboard is a shared pixel canvas. Collapse Technologies may change, freeze, or shut down the board at any time.</p>

<h2>Accounts</h2>
<p>You must sign in to place pixels. You are responsible for activity on your account. One person, one account. We may suspend or ban accounts that break these terms.</p>

<h2>Community standards</h2>
<p>Do not place illegal content, sexual content involving minors, malware, harassment, or material we judge to be abusive. We review reports and may hide, roll back, or quarantine pixels and regions.</p>

<h2>Invites and paint boosts</h2>
<p>Invite codes grant a temporary faster cooldown. They are promotional, not Pixelboard Pro, and we may cap, delay, or revoke them for abuse (self-invites, farms, or spam).</p>

<h2>Pixelboard Pro</h2>
<p>Pro is an optional auto-renewing subscription. It shortens the placement cooldown to one second and unlocks an extended palette plus custom colors. It does not remove the cooldown, and it is not an invite boost.</p>
<p>On the website, Pro is sold through Stripe Checkout. Payment, renewal, and cancellation are handled by Stripe. Manage or cancel in Settings → Manage billing (Stripe Customer Portal). Unused portions of a term are not refundable except as required by Stripe or law.</p>
<p>In the iOS app, Pro is sold through Apple. Payment, renewal, and cancellation are handled by Apple. Manage or cancel in iOS Settings → Apple ID → Subscriptions. Unused portions of a term are not refundable except as required by Apple or law.</p>
<p>Apple product IDs: <code>com.collapsetechnologies.pixelboard.pro.monthly</code> and
    <code>com.collapsetechnologies.pixelboard.pro.annual</code>.</p>

